WEBVTT

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:04.730
The year is 2205 A.D.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:14.240
To annihilate the History Retrograde Army,
who scheme to alter history...

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:19.280
...we, who were born from swords...

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.460
...engage in mortal combat today as well!

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:47.770
"Touken Ranbu Hanamaru S2"

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.130
We're back.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.510
I went with my little brother, um...

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:02.970
I'm Hizamaru, Big Bro!

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.850
...on an expedition.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.640
Here's a souvenir.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.770
"This anime is about the
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:15.990
of a certain group of
Sword Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.660
All right!

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.290
Excuse me!

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.500
Hey, General... I have a request...

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:38.670
That's quite a sigh.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:40.470
Is something the matter?

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:44.050
There are more Sword Warriors
at this citadel now, right?

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:48.890
So that's why Nagasone-<i>niichan</i> moved
into the room I share with Hachisuka-<i>niichan</i>.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.900
But this morning, it happened again--

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.980
Water...

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:06.740
Sorry.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:10.910
That's why fakes are--!

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:12.120
Wh-What?!

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:15.380
I only resigned myself to sharing a room
with you because Urashima said!

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.590
I said sorry, didn't I?

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.800
In the first place, to step over
someone who is sleeping--

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.180
Hey, I'm not done talking yet!

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.050
Come back here!

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:29.020
I just wanted them to get along better...

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:34.020
Well, even brothers compete
and fight with each other.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:39.360
Our former masters, Minamoto no
Yoritomo and Minamoto no Yoshitsune

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.660
did not have much brotherly
love for each other, either.

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:45.410
But no matter what
our former masters were like,

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.030
Big Bro and I get along.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:48.910
Yup, yup, um...

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:50.000
Hizamaru.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.790
...is dear to me, too.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.410
Big Bro!

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:57.880
It's wonderful to get along.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.880
But there's also the saying that
the closer you are, the more you fight.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.840
But I want us all to get along...

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.640
I see. Well, no matter what
kind of Sword Warrior you are,

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:14.600
you are all this father's dear children,
and that will not change.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:15.850
Sorry.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.190
You eat it, Big Bro.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:20.150
At times like this, we can just split it.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:21.740
We're brothers, after all.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.900
Here, um...

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.820
I'm Hizamaru, Big Bro.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:26.950
I know!

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.660
I'll kill you!

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:32.830
Take that!

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.580
You seem really into it!

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.580
I will be the MVP today!

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.210
Since I have something I'm going
to ask my big brothers for later!

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:46.260
Guess what?

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.970
I was the MVP when I was dispatched today!

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.600
That's amazing!

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.520
As expected of my little brother!

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:57.190
So, as a reward, there's something
I want to ask you two...

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.310
What is it?

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.820
Ask me anything!

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.320
I want to eat food
that you two make for me!

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:04.780
Huh?

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.320
Urashima, that's...

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:07.030
All right.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:08.870
Why are you agreeing on your own?

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:12.160
It's fine, isn't it? It's for our
little brother who worked hard.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.790
We can make him some food.

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.750
If that's what you want,
Urashima, I have no choice.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:23.010
I'm really looking forward to it!

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:28.140
I was gonna get some help,

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.850
but Shokudaikiri and Kasen
are both on expeditions.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.930
That's what a fake would do.

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.980
With a real sword like me,
cooking is a simple matter.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:37.810
Well, what will you make?

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.900
I am making this for Urashima.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:45.280
Of course, it will be showy and extravagant!

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:47.240
All right, I have decided.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:49.450
However...

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:54.890
♪ I have no intention 
of making it with you! ♪

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:00.500
♪ Fakes should just go
and make rice or something! ♪

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.250
All right...

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:08.340
♪ First, the stew! The vegetables
should be cut elegantly and beautifully. ♪

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:12.760
♪ It's different from using a sword. ♪

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:17.560
♪ What shape is that? ♪

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:18.980
♪ Cherry blossoms! ♪

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:25.070
♪ Are you blind or something? ♪

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:31.490
♪ If I'm the one doing
the seasoning, then it's easy! ♪

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:36.200
♪ Don't you think there's
too much soy sauce? ♪

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:42.710
♪ This is fine! ♪

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:49.840
♪ Let's heat up the 
oil for the tempura. ♪

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:54.300
♪ If we don't work efficiently,
then it's not beautiful. ♪

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:54.220
"Quickly"    "Plan"
"Speed"    "Efficiency"

00:06:54.300 --> 00:07:00.560
♪ Isn't it dangerous to
put it on the fire so soon? ♪

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:06.650
♪ Unlike you, a fake, I am dexterous. ♪

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:12.030
♪ I can at least do this
much at the same time! ♪

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.740
Next is the savory egg custard!

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:18.040
♪ Put the ingredients in, mix with
soup stock, and put the egg in. ♪

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:22.690
♪ Don't you think there's 
too much in there? ♪

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:36.010
♪ Don't you think Urashima
will be happier if there's a lot inside? ♪

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:39.480
♪ Once this is steamed, it's done! ♪

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:40.390
It's hot!

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:41.980
Don't do anything unnecessary.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:46.270
♪ I don't remember asking
you to do anything! ♪

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:54.910
♪ Most importantly,
for Urashima, who was the MVP, ♪

00:07:54.910 --> 00:08:03.000
♪ we must have a lavish celebration! ♪

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.420
A whole grilled sea bream,
complete with head and tail.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:10.840
♪ Did you remove the scales and guts? ♪

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:16.800
♪ I have my own way of doing things. ♪

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:18.510
Finally, for the tempura!

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:22.390
♪ The oil will splash, so be careful. ♪

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.190
You've been nagging this whole time!

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:26.860
♪ Didn't I tell you not to butt in?! ♪

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:32.400
♪ I was just worried. ♪

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:36.740
♪ And I'm saying that 
that's unnecessary! ♪

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.700
H-Hey!

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.890
Laugh if you wish!

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:04.060
I cannot believe a real sword like
myself can't even make one dish!

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.300
I'm not going to laugh.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:08.770
I can't really cook, either.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:10.520
What will we tell Urashima?

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.610
There's something I used
to make when I first manifested.

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:15.740
A dish my former master used to like.

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.700
If that's okay, then do
you want to make it together?

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:27.500
♪ First, whisk the egg whites
until peaks form. ♪

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.420
♪ How long do I have 
to keep doing this? ♪

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:33.670
♪ Until it's nice and frothy. ♪

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:39.600
♪ Don't you want to serve
Urashima something delicious? ♪

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:44.810
♪ Once peaks form,
add the yolks and whisk more! ♪

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:49.270
♪ Are you sure this will really
become something delicious? ♪

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:51.320
♪ Yes, it'll be fine. ♪

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:54.820
♪ Put the whisked eggs
into the warmed soup stock ♪

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:57.530
♪ and sprinkle some parsley on top ♪

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:01.990
♪ to get fluffy, fluffy eggs! ♪

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:07.780
Wow!

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.670
It's delicious!

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:17.090
It's my first time eating
something so delicious!

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:18.650
I'm glad...

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:21.390
You guys should eat with me, too!

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:25.270
I'm sure it'll be even more
delicious if we eat together!

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.140
Then, I guess I'll have some.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.890
Y-Yeah...

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:30.730
Dinner's ready.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:34.320
I tried a few things
with the food that was left.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:37.650
What're we eating today?

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:40.820
Urashima, whatever
you're eating looks delicious.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:42.780
It <i>is</i> good! But you can't have any!

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:46.790
'Cause my big brothers made this for me!

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:50.920
You're lucky, Urashima.
You've got good brothers.

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:02.510
Hey, fake...

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.720
Thanks for your help today.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:08.510
It wasn't a big deal.

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:10.990
Because yours was ruined.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:13.150
Oh...

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:15.730
However!

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:18.240
It doesn't mean I have accepted you.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.150
A fake's a fake!

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.370
Night.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.250
I'm back!

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:34.710
Welcome back!

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:37.920
--Welcome back!
--Welcome back!

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:40.630
Welcome back, Atsushi.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:41.430
Thanks!

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:49.410
Look at my new form!

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:51.390
So cool!

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:54.060
You have returned looking splendid.

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:56.480
I've definitely come back stronger!

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:59.190
Where did you train?

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:03.160
I went to Kuroda-<i>sama</i>'s place in Chikuzen.

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:06.950
Most of what I learned was the basics of
military tactics and how to use retainers.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:10.500
I think Master has been managing us well,

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:13.710
but I will do my best to be able
to assist when they are not available.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.540
I want to spar with you, Atsushi!

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:22.050
Sure! Let's go to the practice room after
I finish giving my report to Master!

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.510
Atsushi, you're back.

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:30.100
Yeah! I just returned.

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:32.560
Atsushi-<i>san</i>, welcome back!

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.600
Come show us what you learned!

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.480
I'm going to go all out, so be ready!

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:40.730
Should I attack first? Or will you?

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:42.440
It doesn't matter.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:43.900
Then, here I go!

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:55.330
He's completely different
from the old Atsushi.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:56.460
Amazing!

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.170
I-I have lost.

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:03.090
I got one on you!

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:04.470
He's really strong...

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:05.510
That was excellent.

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.010
Hey.

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:09.970
Will you spar with me next?

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:11.930
Sure.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.310
I've been training this whole time.

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:19.820
I won't lose easily!

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:23.940
I'm fighting...

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:24.950
...seriously!

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:27.820
An opening!

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:38.230
All right! I win!

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:40.250
Are you okay?

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:40.840
Huh?

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:41.940
Y-Yeah.

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:44.470
Me next!

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:46.260
I won't lose!

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:49.390
--Right there!
--Go, go!

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:51.220
--I got it!
--Go, go!

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:53.060
--Damn it, you're strong!
--Um...

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:54.740
Hey, Kunihiro!

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.310
You try next!

00:13:57.810 --> 00:13:59.120
Oh, okay!

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:15.410
"Sa"  "Sa"

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:25.590
"54 - Tachi, Oodenta Mitsuyo"

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:25.960
I am one of the Five Great Swords
of Japan, Oodenta Mitsuyo.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:28.340
"55 - Tachi, Sohayanotsurugi"

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:28.550
Sohayanotsurugi Utsusunari...

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:30.550
I am a copy of
Sakanoue's treasured sword.

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:31.800
Nice to meet you.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:36.140
Hey, Brother! I'm glad
we could manifest together!

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:37.020
Yeah.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.020
What's the matter?

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.230
You're a copy, too?

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:44.440
Yup. I'm a copy.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:51.120
Upsy-daisy.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:53.700
Sorry to put you to work
so soon after you arrived.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:57.540
It's fine. I just need to bring
these to the storehouse, right?

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:01.080
Thanks. You'll be a great asset,
Sohayanotsurugi-<i>kun</i>.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.590
Hey! Can you help me with something?

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:06.840
If I can do it after
I carry these over, then sure.

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:08.260
Thanks.

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:10.070
See you later, then.

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:17.930
Jeez, Fudou-<i>chan</i> finishes his drinks so fast.

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:17.930
"Ama"

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:22.400
"Amazake"

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:22.730
It's pretty hard to pour into
these little cups, you know.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.860
Then let me do it.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:27.990
I'm good at copying people's actions,
since I'm a copy.

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:28.860
Just kidding.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.440
--Jeez, what are you saying?
--He said he was a copy.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.690
But he's different from me...

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:37.750
Why?

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.510
Come out.

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:51.880
You've been following me
around lately, haven't you?

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:55.050
Even if I'm a copy, I have spiritual power.

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:57.220
I felt your presence this whole time.

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:03.400
Is there something
you wanted to say to me?

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:07.860
How can you go about like that?

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.690
What do you mean?

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:14.440
You opened up to everyone right away
and found ways to help around the citadel...

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:17.430
Even though you're a copy like me...

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:22.120
How is it that you can be
so unconcerned about being a copy?

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:24.390
It's not that I don't care about it.

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:29.340
But nothing will change
even if I do worry about it.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:31.670
I've been a copy since I was born.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:34.890
Since that's the case,
I can only look forward.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:36.670
What did you say?

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:40.180
It's fine if you start off as a copy.

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:41.920
It's what you do afterward that matters.

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:44.560
The story is proof that you lived.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:51.360
Make your own story.

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:56.910
I'm sure there's something
that you can do because you're you.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:07.330
"Clear Mirror, Still Water"

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:10.300
That Kiyomitsu didn't come today, huh?

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:23.350
Kashuu-<i>san</i>! The food's ready!

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:25.280
I don't want any.

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:29.440
If you're worried about something,
do you want to talk to me about it?

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:30.110
Huh?

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:36.200
I might not be as reliable as
Yamatonokami-<i>san</i>, but I'm good at helping.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:43.810
You know, I haven't been dispatched once
since I was dispatched to Sunomata in January.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:48.280
Even so, I train desperately every day,
trying to become stronger.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.840
But then, I lost so fast against Atsushi
when he came back from his training.

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:56.130
That was just one match!

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:59.180
Kashuu-<i>san</i>, you're amazing, too!

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:01.810
Master entrusted the care of
the new Sword Warriors to you,

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:04.220
and you've been working hard at it--

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:08.190
That's just because
I was the first sword here!

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:09.360
That's not--

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:12.820
A sword's duty--our duty--is to fight, right?

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:17.450
Then what worth do I have
when I am not allowed to fight?

00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:21.950
I'm not necessary to this citadel,
or to Master, anymore!

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:23.910
That's not true!

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:27.710
Sorry!

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:30.420
Kashuu-<i>san</i>, wait!

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:35.300
What I can do because I'm me...

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:36.010
Sorry...

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:37.510
Kashuu-<i>san</i>!

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:44.350
What's the matter with Kashuu?

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:45.330
Actually...

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:52.650
Is that what happened?

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:55.180
I wanted to comfort him...

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:58.860
I'm not good at talking, but...

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.590
...I'm the only one who can tell him.

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:11.850
Sulking and then taking it out on Horikawa...

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:15.250
I'm not cute at all right now.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:20.590
What should I do?

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:23.930
Why aren't you here at a time like this,

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:25.810
Yasusada?

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:34.940
You dropped this.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:37.780
Yamanbagiri...

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.270
Th-Thanks...

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.280
The reason you aren't getting chosen
to be on the teams sent out

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:46.800
is that you are strong.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.200
Huh? What are you saying?

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:53.540
The day you were made responsible
for the new Sword Warriors,

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:54.920
I was the attendant.

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:59.300
"Kashuu has been at the citadel the longest

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:02.930
and has more dispatch experience
than anyone else. He surpasses everyone.

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:08.610
That's why I'll dispatch the others
until they catch up to him."

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:10.390
That's what Master said.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:15.020
I'm not strong. I even lost to Atsushi.

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:18.610
Strength on the battlefield
isn't just about swordsmanship.

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:23.820
I think tactics and teamwork 
are also important.

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:28.580
Then, why was I chosen to take
care of the new Sword Warriors?

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:32.580
That's because you are kind.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:36.490
Master thought that Sword Warriors
who just manifested and were uneasy

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:40.690
would feel comfortable if they were with you.

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:45.550
I see... I'm glad...

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:48.180
It's not because Master doesn't like me...

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:52.890
It probably won't make you
happy hearing it from a copy like me,

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:56.300
but... you're doing a good job.

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:59.360
It's something you can
do because you're you.

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:04.820
Thanks. I feel better thanks
to you, Yamanbagiri.

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:11.500
Speaking of which, you're not wearing
the hood you always have on. What happened?

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:12.300
Huh?!

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:14.620
Nothing!

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:17.610
What? But your face is 
so pretty, I'm jealous.

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:20.530
D-Don't call me pretty!

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:28.580
Today's moon is beautiful.

00:21:29.560 --> 00:21:30.490
Mikazuki...

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:34.940
I haven't talked to you up
here since last year, huh?

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:37.440
That time, Yamatonokami was here, too.

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:43.150
Yeah. Jeez, that Yasusada.
Where the heck has he been wandering?

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:47.450
Since Master hasn't said anything,
I'm sure he's doing well.

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:52.540
Seeing your face, it looks like you've
worked out what was bothering you.

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:54.830
Oh, you noticed?

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:57.370
Aw man, I'm so uncool...

00:21:57.710 --> 00:22:01.090
That's not true. The young should worry.

00:22:01.670 --> 00:22:03.900
You really do talk like an old man.

00:22:04.630 --> 00:22:06.430
Because I am one.

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:11.060
Kashuu, you've become kind.

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:19.310
Not really. I've always been kind.

00:22:19.310 --> 00:22:20.720
That's true.

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:24.650
That's good, that's good.

00:23:55.030 --> 00:24:01.590
"More <i>Hanamaru</i> Next Week!!"
